cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kestrel in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Kestrel: Memory-Tiered Local LLM Inference across VRAM, RAM and NVMe"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Kestrel Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eduardo7125/kestrel"
url: "https://github.com/eduardo7125/kestrel"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM inference
  - offloading
  - NVMe
  - memory tiering
  - mixture of experts
  - GGUF
  - llama.cpp
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  Kestrel is a local LLM inference runtime that profiles the machine and the
  model, builds an explicit execution plan placing each tensor group in VRAM,
  RAM or NVMe, and executes it with an inference-specific memory scheduler:
  budgeted allocation, prefetching, Belady-optimal residency for dense layers
  and an expert-granular cache for Mixture-of-Experts models.
